{#- The score template vLLM serves for ctxl-rerank-v2-instruct-multilingual-6b (recipe.yaml).

    Two render contexts, one output byte string:
    - the engine (vLLM's /rerank): the template receives `messages` -- exactly two messages,
      roles "query" and "document" -- and the request's instruction as a template kwarg;
    - the CPU equivalence harness: it renders this file with flat `query` / `document` /
      `instruction` kwargs, so the flat branch mirrors the engine's render for the same texts.

    No BOS line: this checkpoint's tokenizer post-processor already prepends <s> (id 1) to the
    rendered prompt under vLLM's fixed add_special_tokens=True; the vendor template's bos_token
    line would emit it twice (measured ids [1, 1, ...] vs the reference's [1, ...]).

    The instruction (the model card's inline form, " {instruction}" before " ??") reaches the
    prompt only through the kwarg or a system message. This recipe's client declares
    instruction: none and never sends the field, so the branch is inert for the served path. -#}
{%- if query is defined and document is defined -%}
{%- set query_text = query -%}
{%- set document_text = document -%}
{%- else -%}
{%- set query_text = messages | selectattr("role", "eq", "query") | map(attribute="content") | first -%}
{%- set document_text = messages | selectattr("role", "eq", "document") | map(attribute="content") | first -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- if instruction is defined -%}
{%- set instruction_text = instruction -%}
{%- else -%}
{%- set instruction_text = messages | selectattr("role", "eq", "system") | map(attribute="content") | first | default("") -%}
{%- endif -%}
Check whether a given document contains information helpful to answer the query.
<Document> {{ document_text }}
<Query> {{ query_text }}{% if instruction_text %} {{ instruction_text }}{% endif %} ??